            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Technically this patch needs to be ran against rf_service_validator individually. However, based on the ordering of the patches this is not possible. \n\nI guess you can just state here that you validated the route in the final patch of the series, else you would need to reorder and validate each patch separately."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "> Technically this patch needs to be ran against rf_service_validator individually\n\ndoes it?  why?  This patch doesn't add any (discoverable) endpoints.\n\nI'm only asking because I seem to have made all the wrong assumptions about patch structure when contributing to bmcweb, and perhaps, using your answer, I can make a documentation update to make things more clear."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "> does it?  why?  This patch doesn't add any (discoverable) endpoints.\n\nI guess that is fair to say. \n\n> I seem to have made all the wrong assumptions\n\nI don't think so, it's just important that the whole series strictly has to go in together which seems fine. \n\nEvery patch adds new routes, but doesn't make any statement on validation, that's mainly my point."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "requires https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/libcper/+/86542"
